+# xz 5.8.4 on Windows ARM64, aarch64-pc-cygwin (MSYS2 runtime) build
+# Host: Qualcomm Snapdragon (ARMv8, Family 8 Model 1), Windows 11 10.0.26100, native ARM64
+# Date: 2026-11-23. Another job (a GNU tar test suite, -j8) was running on the
+# host at the same time, so end-to-end timings are noisy; the CRC32
+# microbenchmark (best of N) is the most stable number.
+#
+# Variants (same machine, same session):
+#   base = pre-port package binaries from the aarch64 sysroot
+#          (C:/msys64/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin; cross conf CFLAGS="-pipe", i.e. -O0)
+#   ctl  = unpatched main branch, -O2 (configure default), msys-lzma-5.dll only;
+#          isolates the effect of the arm64-port CRC32 change
+#   new  = arm64-port branch, -O2, build-arm64 (hardware CRC32 via runtime detection)
+#
+# Input: deterministic 64 MiB (48 MiB repo text repeated + 16 MiB Python random.Random(42))
+#   sha256 ff4355579cc00446c7f4e9485db502beff07e1283ec7b52a8abe9ab9b019a751
+#
+## 1. lzma_crc32() microbenchmark, 256 MiB buffer, best of 5-7 runs
+# variant  run                      MiB/s
+base       crc32-256MiB             615.1   (run 2: 675.9)
+ctl        crc32-256MiB             1681.0
+new        crc32-256MiB             6254.5  (run 1: 7784.8)
+# crc32 value identical for all variants: 3bcd384b
+# new vs ctl: 3.7x (hardware CRC32 instructions vs generic slice-by-8, both -O2)
+#
+## 2. End-to-end xz, 64 MiB input, 5 interleaved runs, wall time in ms (median / min)
+# op        variant  median  min
+c6          base     34783   30279    # xz -T1 -6 -c
+c6          new      17992   14549
+d6          base     336     317      # xz -dc (of the -6 output)
+d6          new      252     197
+c0crc32     base     10140   8421     # xz -T1 -0 --check=crc32 -c
+c0crc32     new      4163    3487
+t0crc32     base     1972    1537     # xz -t (on the -0 --check=crc32 file)
+t0crc32     new      672     572
+# base->new end-to-end gains are dominated by -O0 -> -O2, not by the CRC change.
+#
+## 3. CRC change in isolation (ctl vs new, same xz.exe, both -O2), ms median / min
+c0crc32     ctl      5581    3794
+c0crc32     new      6065    4053
+t0crc32     ctl      841     639
+t0crc32     new      890     623
+# Within run-to-run noise (CRC32 is a small share of these ops); the expected
+# saving is ~28 ms of CRC time per 64 MiB checked.
+# Round-trip check: base decodes new's .xz and new decodes base's .xz -> identical to input.
